    {
      "id": "lin7167",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Constitutional Articles Related to Vice President"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Article 63 of the Indian Constitution provides for the office of the Vice President of India.",
        "The Vice President is elected by an electoral college consisting of members of both Houses of Parliament through proportional representation.",
        "Qualifications require being an Indian citizen, at least 35 years of age, and qualified for election to the Rajya Sabha.",
        "Serves a 5-year term and functions as the ex-officio Chairman of the Rajya Sabha.",
        "Acts as President during a vacancy caused by resignation, removal, death, or inability of the President.",
        "Removal procedure requires a resolution passed by a majority of all the then members of the Rajya Sabha and agreed to by the Lok Sabha."
      ],
      "id": "renmbxw"
    },
